    "evidence_text": " She was in several movies including \"Blue Hawaii\", \"The Singing Nun\" and \"Monster on the Campus\".\n\nKatrina Conder is an Australian television presenter.\n\n She was a host Channel Nine's late night game show Quizmania.\n\n Katrina has also appeared on 3 episodes of Blue Heelers as a nurse.\n\n Katrina starred in a lead role in the 2005/06 9minds production of Black Rock\n\nThe Singing Nun (film)\nThe Singing Nun is a 1966 American semi-biographical film about the life of Jeanine Deckers, a nun who recorded the chart-topping hit song \"Dominique\".\n It starred Debbie Reynolds in the title role.\n The film also stars Ricardo Montalb\u00e1n, Katharine Ross, Chad Everett, and Ed Sullivan as himself.\n It was Henry Koster's final directing job.\n\n The film stars C\u00e9cile de France as Jeannine Deckers, also known as The Singing Nun).\n\nKatharine Juliet Ross (born January 29, 1940) is an American film and stage actress.\n\n She won a Golden Globe for \"Voyage of the Damned\" (1976).",
